WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.467
-Our next guest
is a talented actress

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.267
you know from her work
in "Bring It On",

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:06.000
"Being Mary Jane,"
and "The Inspection."

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.133
She stars in the third season
of "Truth Be Told,"

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.868
which is streaming
on Apple TV+,

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.434
with new episodes
released on Fridays.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:12.901
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:15.467
-The superintendent shut me down
from asking questions at school

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:18.868
or even acknowledging
anything's wrong.

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:23.133
All the memorials around town,
they're all for Emily.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:26.267
It's like Drea
didn't even exist.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.834
I need to act.

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:29.300
♪♪

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.534
-You are.

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:33.734
With those bright young minds
you mold.

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:34.968
-Well, what use are their minds

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.934
if I can't keep
their bodies safe?

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:39.901
-Please welcome back to the show
Gabrielle Union, everyone!

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:51.834
♪♪

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:56.234
♪♪

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.501
It's so wonderful
to have you back.

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:00.400
-Thank you.
That was a very warm welcome.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.467
-Yeah, it's a very warm crowd
tonight.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.300
-Yes.
-This is --

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.634
It's a very intense show.

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.067
This is the third season
of a show.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:10.701
Octavia Spencer
plays a crime podcaster.

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.834
You play a principal
in an area

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:15.000
where there's a lot of kids
being trafficked.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.567
It must be a very intense thing
to take on.

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:20.100
-Incredibly intense.
-And how was the --

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.100
I know you've worked
with Octavia Spencer before.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.267
That must make it
a little easier

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:24.734
to take on material like this.

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:26.601
-Yeah, there's no way I could
do this show without Octavia.

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:28.667
We have been friends
literally forever.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.400
Over -- well over 20 years.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.000
'Cause it's crazy
'cause we're only 27.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.033
[ Laughter ]
But we've friends for so long.

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:37.167
We started on a show called
"City of Angels."

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.767
-Oh, yeah.
-And it was me and Octavia

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:42.234
and Viola Davis
and Maya Rudolph,

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:45.067
who before she went off to do
that show that you guys do.

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.367
-It did not go well for her.

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:47.934
-You know,
I think it worked out.

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:50.467
-But, yeah, we all met
on that show and bonded.

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:54.067
And, you know, from there,
that trust grew.

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:56.934
So when she hit me and was like,
"I have a great opportunity

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:59.934
for you to join season 3
of 'Truth be Told,'

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:01.701
but it's some
really tough material.

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:04.234
But I think you are uniquely
prepared for this."

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.734
And when I read the script,

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:09.067
I was like,
"This is gonna be a gut punch."

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:11.067
Every day, you know,
it's gonna be

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:13.767
a little triggering
or a lot triggering.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.667
But for the greater good
of getting --

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.200
like, to create
a bigger platform

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.801
to let more people know
that human trafficking,

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:22.300
sexual trafficking
is a global pandemic.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.634
And when Black and Brown girls
go missing,

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:28.334
we do not have the resources
or the media attention.

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:33.000
And we are often demonized
and sort of --

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.367
are held complicit
in our own abuse.

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:38.467
And just trying to, you know,
recenter the focus

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.701
on the most marginalized
of the marginalized.

00:02:40.701 --> 00:02:43.567
-Before you became an actor,
you actually were thinking about

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:44.901
being a lawyer.
-Yeah.

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:46.367
-Which just seems very similar
to what you were just

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:48.234
talking about.
How far down the line

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.067
did you go with is that?
-Well, you know, I, um...

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:51.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:53.834
The thing about
standardized testing...

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:55.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:59.801
I was studying for the LSATs
and not doing well at all.

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:02.534
And I got an internship
at a modeling agency

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:04.634
at the same time
as I was taking these LSATs.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:08.033
And when my modeling agency,
you know, gig internship ended,

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:10.234
they were like,
"Would you ever consider

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:12.734
being one of our girls"?

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:17.434
And I'm looking at the LSATs
that I'm doing terribly at

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:20.133
or being in a Tupac video,
and I was like, "I..."

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.601
-I gotta be honest, even if
you were crushing the LSATs...

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:25.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:28.067
-I'm going with Tupac.
-Yeah.

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:30.267
-Yeah. So, I went into
the entertainment business,

00:03:30.267 --> 00:03:33.367
and I kind of left
the dream of law behind.

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:35.467
-Now, you have a 4-year-old,

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:37.901
and I know it's very early
to tell, but there maybe

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:39.934
is a bit of entertainer in her.

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:41.734
-Oh, a lot of entertainer
in her.

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:45.067
-She gave a -- now, I have a
6-year-old, I have a 4-year-old.

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:47.667
I can't imagine either of them
having the wherewithal

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:50.000
or the nerve to give a toast
at my birthday party.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.601
But your 4-year-old
gave a toast?

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:55.133
-Oh, a full toast.
Like, she has --

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:57.767
Like she's Iyanla.
So, this is, like --

00:03:57.767 --> 00:03:59.567
We're in Africa.
It's late.

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:02.033
We're in Tanzania.
And she was like,

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:04.767
"Mommy, you are worthy."
And I was like...

00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:06.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:09.000
"How do you know I struggle
with feelings of worthlessness?"

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.834
[ Laughter ]
Like...

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:13.667
But she never turns down --
-On a microphone?

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.601
-On a microphone
in front of a crowd.

00:04:15.601 --> 00:04:18.300
-Planned, or did she just kinda
go up and ask the emcee,

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.467
"I'd love to say a few words"?
-Well, anytime a --

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.100
Anytime a microphone comes out,
she's like,

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.901
"Yes, I'd like to have a word."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:25.801
-And so we're like, "Kaav,
what would you like to say?"

00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:26.934
And we're thinking it's gonna be

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:28.834
some cutesy toddler
"Happy birthday."

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:31.000
But, she was like,
"And for my third point..."

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.200
[ Laughter ]
And she had like, you know,

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:36.200
the Dead Sea Scrolls
of points she wanted to make.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:40.067
But, no, she's very articulate,
and she loves to public-speak

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:42.968
and sing and do all the things.
-That is a huge thing.

00:04:42.968 --> 00:04:45.868
Because I think,
even for people --

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.534
even for children who to go on
to be performers,

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:49.234
they have to get over that
public-speaking thing first.

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:50.701
So the fact
that she's already there...

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:52.100
-Oh, no,
she's ready to do press.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:54.901
-She's like, "Hey, Seth.
Anyway, you are worthy."

00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:56.701
[ Laughter ]
"For my next song..."

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:58.701
-My kids once very sweetly,
right before bed said,

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:00.067
"One day,
you'll be worthy, Dad,"

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:01.434
and I thought that was nice.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:04.767
-They said, "One day."
-Gives me something to aim for.

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:06.567
-Now, you are married to --

00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:07.934
I know he's a former athlete,

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:09.267
but every time I see
the two of you together,

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:11.434
I just want to say,
"Two fashion icons."

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:13.033
-He's cute.
-All right, that's Dwyane Wade.

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:14.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:17.501
And, you know, --

00:05:17.501 --> 00:05:18.801
And I'm wondering what life --

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:22.000
And I know he's still involved
in sports ownership,

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.634
but do you, as a family,
do you yourself still watch

00:05:25.634 --> 00:05:27.934
and root for sports,
post-playing career?

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:29.400
-Oh, yes.
-All right.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.734
-I have a problem.
I become everybody's Mama June.

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:33.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:36.033
So, we have, like --
We have a suite at SoFi,

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:37.501
so we watch the Chargers
and the Rams.

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:41.100
And I have to say,
the Rams with Odell?

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:45.200
All the women in my group chat
are like, "I am a Rams fan."

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.934 --> 00:05:49.267
But, I'm like, "Girl,
you are an Odell fan."

00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:50.467
No one comes that early.

00:05:50.467 --> 00:05:52.234
But they're like,
"He's stretching."

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:55.367
[ Laughter ]
"Get those hammies, Odell."

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:58.133
But, yeah.
But this year, not as much.

00:05:58.133 --> 00:05:59.868
And I grew up in the Bay Area.

00:05:59.868 --> 00:06:01.467
I'm from Omaha, Nebraska,
where we don't have

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:02.767
a professional team.
-Yeah.

00:06:02.767 --> 00:06:04.234
-But everyone's Cornhusker fans.

00:06:04.234 --> 00:06:06.968
But growing up in the Bay Area,
you're a 49er fan.

00:06:06.968 --> 00:06:08.968
So we've been watching
the 49ers.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.634
-That's nice,
to have a rooting interest

00:06:10.634 --> 00:06:12.968
going into championship weekend.
That's a nice feeling.

00:06:12.968 --> 00:06:15.100
-Well, again,
with the group chat.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.133
So, apparently,
the group chat is all --

00:06:17.133 --> 00:06:19.534
throwing all of our weight
behind Jalen Hurts.

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:22.167
-Oh, interesting.
He's the handsome this year?

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:26.200
-Apparently, he is.
He -- He does well for himself.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.467 --> 00:06:29.100
I'd like to go home
to a happy home,

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.868
so I'm not gonna comment there.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.868 --> 00:06:35.100
But the streets are saying...
-The streets.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.534
Look, you're hearing things,
you're not saying things.

00:06:37.534 --> 00:06:38.834
You're hearing things.

00:06:38.834 --> 00:06:41.234
-For the older kids,
he's like the new Warren Moon.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:43.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.868 --> 00:06:46.667
-For the way older kids,
or I guess just me.

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:48.767
-You got me.
-I got you. I totally --.

00:06:48.767 --> 00:06:51.300
And you mentioned you're
from Omaha, and a big family.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.567
-Very big.
-So a lot of family

00:06:52.567 --> 00:06:53.834
still in Omaha.
-Yeah.

00:06:53.834 --> 00:06:55.701
The bulk of our family
is still in Omaha.

00:06:55.701 --> 00:06:58.434
We have the largest Black family
in the state of Nebraska.

00:06:58.434 --> 00:07:00.434
-Oh, my goodness.
Congratulations.

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:01.934
-I don't know how hard that is.
[ Scattered applause ]

00:07:01.934 --> 00:07:03.868
-Okay.
[ Both laugh ]

00:07:03.868 --> 00:07:05.334
-But one of the largest
in the Midwest.

00:07:05.334 --> 00:07:06.601
And this -- this last summer,

00:07:06.601 --> 00:07:08.801
we had our 105th annual
family reunion.

00:07:08.801 --> 00:07:12.567
-105th annual fam--
That is an incredible number.

00:07:12.567 --> 00:07:14.167
-Yes, we're called
the Dozens of Cousins.

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:16.701
-Dozens of Cousins.
-Yeah, the Bryant-Fisher family.

00:07:16.701 --> 00:07:18.934
-Now, you're doing something
that I find --

00:07:18.934 --> 00:07:22.000
I actually find very impressive
and I hope does not come to pass

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.868
for 50 years from now.
-Uh-oh.

00:07:25.868 --> 00:07:27.334
-You are planning
your own funeral.

00:07:27.334 --> 00:07:29.000
-Oh, yes.
-Okay. This is something --

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.868
-You have to.
-When did you decide

00:07:30.868 --> 00:07:32.167
to start putting
the planning into it?

00:07:32.167 --> 00:07:34.267
-Going to a lot of bad funerals,
and it's...

00:07:34.267 --> 00:07:35.868
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.868 --> 00:07:38.868
-It's kind of like when me and
my husband were getting married,

00:07:38.868 --> 00:07:40.934
like, the couple summers
before we got married,

00:07:40.934 --> 00:07:43.634
we were at --
at other people's weddings,

00:07:43.634 --> 00:07:46.834
like, "Not that, never that,
nope, nope, nope."

00:07:46.834 --> 00:07:50.501
So it led me to, like, think,
"I feel like I need to plan

00:07:50.501 --> 00:07:53.434
my funeral down to,
like, the smallest detail."

00:07:53.434 --> 00:07:55.767
So I've chosen
all of the sexiest photos.

00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:57.200
I don't want like --
If I die at 88,

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.467
I don't want to be 88
on the program.

00:07:59.467 --> 00:08:02.000
You give me --
You give me my thirst traps.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.701
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.701 --> 00:08:05.400
All my best material.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:06.901
But, like, I've got playlists
that they have.

00:08:06.901 --> 00:08:08.767
Like, food.
Like, I want a good funeral.

00:08:08.767 --> 00:08:09.901
-That's great.
-Yeah.

00:08:09.901 --> 00:08:11.701
-And now, when you mention
a playlist,

00:08:11.701 --> 00:08:13.968
are you constantly editing it?
-You have to.

00:08:13.968 --> 00:08:15.300
-If you hear a new banger,
are you like,

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:18.534
"Oh, that's gotta be..."
-Now we have a lot of Beyoncé

00:08:18.534 --> 00:08:19.901
from the latest.
-Yeah.

00:08:19.901 --> 00:08:21.801
-You have to constantly update.
-Do you let her know?

00:08:21.801 --> 00:08:24.601
Are you like, "Good news.
You're on of my funeral mix."

00:08:24.601 --> 00:08:26.901
-Listen, when I showed up
at her birthday, and I'm like,

00:08:26.901 --> 00:08:29.901
"It's a circle of life,
and I just want you to know

00:08:29.901 --> 00:08:32.367
that when it's the end for me,
you'll also be there."

00:08:32.367 --> 00:08:33.767
[ Laughter ]

00:08:33.767 --> 00:08:35.801
-That does seem like a thing
that might be hard to hear,

00:08:35.801 --> 00:08:38.501
which is like, "I'm gonna
play you at my funeral."

00:08:38.501 --> 00:08:40.601
[ Laughter ]
But there you go.

00:08:40.601 --> 00:08:42.434
I think that's very nice
that you put that work into it

00:08:42.434 --> 00:08:44.033
because I think that --
you know, obviously,

00:08:44.033 --> 00:08:46.534
when that happens, you,
for your loved one

00:08:46.534 --> 00:08:48.000
that recently passed,
you want to make sure

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.934
you do it the way they did.
-And I think we think

00:08:49.934 --> 00:08:51.901
we are closer to people
than we actually are.

00:08:51.901 --> 00:08:53.534
-Yeah.
-Have you ever heard yourself

00:08:53.534 --> 00:08:55.133
described by a family member?

00:08:55.133 --> 00:08:56.634
And you're like,
"Do you know me?"

00:08:56.634 --> 00:08:57.834
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:57.834 --> 00:09:00.534
-Like, at what point
do you know me?

00:09:00.534 --> 00:09:02.934
-I know,
based on what I've heard,

00:09:02.934 --> 00:09:05.234
your daughter will be there
being like, "She was worthy."

00:09:05.234 --> 00:09:07.300
[ Laughter ]

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:08.601
You know what?
That's what you should do.

00:09:08.601 --> 00:09:10.367
You should also write
the speeches people give

00:09:10.367 --> 00:09:12.200
at your funeral.
Just like, "Don't go off book."

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:13.801
-Yeah, like,
"I've prepared some remarks."

00:09:13.801 --> 00:09:15.300
[ Laughter ]
Read that.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:16.434
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:09:16.434 --> 00:09:17.801
It's always such a pleasure
to see you.

00:09:17.801 --> 00:09:20.033
You guys,
that's Gabrielle Union.

00:09:20.033 --> 00:09:22.100
"Truth Be Told"
is streaming on Apple TV+

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:23.701
with new episodes
released on Fridays.

00:09:23.701 --> 00:09:25.300
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

